    "result_text": "There is only one test class in the project (the acceptance test), and it passes along with the full build.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the daily owner-creation limit on `POST /api/owners`: creating an owner is now rejected with **429 Too Many Requests** once 100 or more owners share the new owner's `registrationDate`.\n\nChanges, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (mirroring the existing `RequireCityCapacity` capacity rule):\n\n- **`RequireDailyOwnerLimit`** (function) \u2014 after `DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate` populates the date, counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals the new owner's, throwing `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` at 100+.\n- **`DailyOwnerLimitExceededException`** \u2014 a checked exception (`extends Exception`) so it appears in the `throws` clause.\n- **`DailyOwnerLimitExceededExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds `429` with an `{\"errors\":[\"registrationDate\"]}` body, matching the shape of the existing capacity handler.\n- **Escalation YAML** wiring the exception to its handler.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted a `dailyLimit` step between `registrationDate` and `build`, under the same `transaction` governance as the rest of the pipeline.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreRejectsOverDailyLimit` (creates 100 owners dated today, expects the 101st to be `429`) and the full build pass green.",
